Задание №2 - 24-11-2026 - download-assignments.py
The file download_assignments.py is a Python script designed to download external assignment links from a README.md file, save them as local Markdown files, and update the README.md to point to these local copies. It includes robust concurrency control, platform-specific fetchers, and a detailed parser for the README structure.
Below are the definitions and references for the primary functions and symbols in the file.
Global Constants and Configuration
Symbol	Type	Definition / Purpose
README_PATH	Path	Path to the README.md file, located two directories up from the script.
REPO_ROOT	Path	Root directory of the repository (parent of README_PATH).
LOCK_FILE	Path	Path to the lock file (.download_assignments.lock) used to prevent concurrent script execution.
SECTION_TO_DIR	dict[str, str]	Maps human-readable section names from the README (e.g., "Backend", "Python") to local directory names (e.g., "backend", "python").
SKIP_URL_PATTERNS	list[str]	List of domain substrings for platforms that cannot be reliably fetched without authentication (e.g., Google Drive, Notion, Dropbox).
GITHUB_TOKEN	str	Environment variable for a GitHub personal access token to increase API rate limits.
